This package thus lays the groundwork for computing with Dold-Puppe extensions
of nonlinear functors, deriving nonlinear functors, and also allows any
endofunctor of R-modules implemented in Macaulay2 to immediately be canonically
extended to an endofunctor at the level of chain complexes. Moreover, almost
all methods are implemented with an eye toward user accessibility and
comprehension of the outputs. This is illustrated in many of the documentation
nodes below.

Getting started:
================

  * *note The Dold-Kan Correspondence in Macaulay2: The Dold-Kan Correspondence
    in Macaulay2, -- compute the image of a non-negatively graded complex under
    the Dold-Kan correspondence
  * *note Making simplicial modules: Making simplicial modules, -- information
    about the basic constructors
  * *note Making maps between simplicial modules: Making maps between
    simplicial modules, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note Basic invariants and properties: Basic invariants and properties, --
    information about accessing basic features
  * *note face/degeneracy maps of a simplicial module: face/degeneracy maps of
    a simplicial module, -- access the face and degeneracy maps of a simplicial
    module

