exteriorInclusion -- computes the image of the 2nd exterior power into the tensor product
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        exteriorInclusion(S)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, or *note Complex:
        (Complexes)Complex, or *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, optional
        integer argument specifies top degree
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, or *note
        Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the map representing the image of the
        2nd exterior power of $S$ into the tensor product $S \otimes S$.

Description
===========

Given a simplicial module $S$ (or a complex), this function computes the map
$$\bigwedge^2 S \to S \otimes S,$$ The cokernel of this map is by definition
the second symmetric power of $S$. This method is mainly used in conjunction
with the *note tensorLES: tensorLES, command to compute induced maps on
homology for canonical short exact sequences.

