extPower -- compute the Dold-Puppe extension of the exterior power functor to simplicial modules
************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        extPower(d, S, Options => {Degeneracy => false, TopDegree => null})
  * Inputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, An integer representing the
        degree of the exterior power.
      * S, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, A simplicial module to
        which the exterior power functor extension is applied.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degeneracy: extPower_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegeneracy=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => a
        *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false,
        Default value is false. Indicates whether to include degeneracy maps in
        the construction.
      * *note TopDegree: extPower_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTopDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => an
        *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, Default is null.
        If provided, specifies the top degree for the construction of the
        simplicial module.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, The Dold-Puppe extension
        of the exterior power functor applied to the simplicial module S.

Description
===========

This function computes the Dold-Puppe extension of the exterior power functor
to the category of chain complexes. It can be applied to a simplicial module, a
complex, or maps thereof. This method is equivalent to using *note schurMap:
schurMap, for the partition $(1, 1, \dots , 1)$, but is generally much faster.

