forgetComplex(SimplicialModule) -- forget the underlying complex data of a simplicial module obtained as a Dold-Kan image
*************************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note forgetComplex: forgetComplex_lpSimplicialModule_rp,
  * Usage: 
        forgetComplex(S)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, A simplicial module,
        which is assumed to be obtained as a Dold-Kan image.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note RememberSummands:
        forgetComplex_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmRememberSummands=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => a *note
        Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value true, Default
        value is true. Indicates whether to remember the component summands of
        the simplicial module when creating the new simplicial module.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, A new simplicial module
        that is no longer viewed as a Dold-Kan image of some complex

Description
===========

This function removes the data of the underlying complex from a simplicial
module $S$ that is obtained as a Dold-Kan image. The function checks if the
simplicial module has an associated complex and, if so, it reconstructs the
simplicial module without the complex data while preserving the face and
degeneracy maps.

If the option `RememberSummands` is set to true (the default), the function
will remember the summands of the simplicial module when reconstructing it. The
face and degeneracy maps of the original simplicial module are preserved in the
new simplicial module. This function is good for testing that the normalization
of the Dold-Kan functor recovers the original complex, since the *note
normalize: (SchurFunctors)normalize, command by default first checks if a
simplicial module is obtained as a Dold-Kan image before attempting a more
costly computation.

