isCommutative(SimplicialModuleMap) -- whether a simplicial module map commutes with the face/degeneracy maps
************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isCommutative: (Macaulay2Doc)isCommutative,
  * Usage: 
        isCommutative f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when $f$
        commutes with the face/degeneracy maps

Description
===========

For a simplicial module map $f : C \to D$, this method checks whether, for all
$i$, we have $dd^D_{i} * f_i =  f_{i-1} * dd^C_i$ and, if the source at target
are equipped with degeneracy maps, it also checks the equality $ss^D_{i} * f_i
=  f_{i+1} * ss^C_i$.

We first construct a random simplicial module map which commutes with the
face/degeneracy map.

