isSimplicialMorphism(SimplicialModuleMap) -- whether a simplicial module map is a morphism of simplicial modules
****************************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isSimplicialMorphism:
    isSimplicialMorphism_lpSimplicialModuleMap_rp,
  * Usage: 
        isSimplicialMorphism f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when $f$
        commutes with the face/degeneracy maps and has degree $0$

Description
===========

For a simplicial module map $f : C \to D$ of degree $d$, this method checks
whether $d = 0$ and, for all $i$, we have $dd^D_{i+d} * f_i =  f_{i-1} *
dd^C_i$ and if the simplicial module also has degeneracy maps, it checks that
$ss^D_{i} * f_i =  f_{i+1} * ss^C_i$.

We first construct a random simplicial module morphism.

+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c];                                                   |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = simplicialModule(freeResolution coker vars S, Degeneracy => true)|
|                                                                          |
|      1      4      10      20                                            |
|o2 = S  <-- S  <-- S   <-- S  <-- ...                                     |
|                                                                          |
|     0      1      2       3                                              |
|                                                                          |
|o2 : SimplicialModule                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = C ** C                                                           |
|                                                                          |
|      1      16      100      400                                         |
|o3 = S  <-- S   <-- S    <-- S   <-- ...                                  |
|                                                                          |
|     0      1       2        3                                            |
|                                                                          |
|o3 : SimplicialModule                                                     |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f1 = randomSimplicialMap(D, C, Cycle => true, InternalDegree => 1);  |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isSimplicialMorphism f1                                              |
|                                                                          |
|o5 = true                                                                 |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(degree f1 == 0)                                               |
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------+

We next generate a complex morphism that (likely) induces a nontrivial map on
homology.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : f2 = randomSimplicialMap(D, C, Cycle => true);                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : isSimplicialMorphism f2                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(degree f2 == 0)                                                  |
