isWellDefined(SimplicialModule) -- whether a simplicial module is well-defined
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when C
        determines a well defined simplicial module

Description
===========

This routine checks that the face/degeneracy maps of C satisfy the simplicial
identities (see *note isSimplicialModule:
isSimplicialModule_lpSimplicialModule_rp, for a list of these identities). If
there are no degeneracy maps stored, it instead checks that the naive
normalization of C is a well-defined complex. Additionally, it checks that the
underlying data in C is a properly formed *note SimplicialModule:
SimplicialModule, object in Macaulay2. If the variable debugLevel is set to a
value greater than zero, then information about the nature of any failure is
displayed.

As a first example, we construct the Dold-Kan image of a free resolution and
verify that it is well-defined.

