This method also checks the following aspects of the data structure:

  * The underlying hash table has exactly the expected keys, namely, source,
    target, degree, map, cache
  * The ring of the source and target are the same
  * The source and target are well defined simplicial modules
  * The degree is an integer
  * All keys in the map field are integers or sequences, in the range of the
    top degree of the source
  * The source and target of each $f_i$ is as expected
  * If the isCommutative key is present in the cache table, then commutativity
    of the map with the face/degeneracy maps is checked

