kernel(SimplicialModuleMap) -- make the kernel of a map of simplicial modules
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note kernel: (Macaulay2Doc)kernel,
  * Usage: 
        kernel f
        ker f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeLimit (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * Strategy (missing documentation) => ..., default value {}, 
      * *note SubringLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)kernel_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSubringLimit=>_
        pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value infinity,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, 

Description
===========

The kernel of a simplicial module map $f : C \to D$ is the simplicial module
$E$ whose $i$-th term is $kernel(f_i)$, and whose face/degeneracy map is
induced from the face/degeneracy map on the source.

