|                                 |
|o11 = true                       |
+---------------------------------+

This is the primary constructor used by all of the more user friendly methods
for constructing a simplicial module map.

Caveat
======

This constructor minimizes computation and does very little error checking. To
verify that a simplicial module map is well constructed, use *note
isWellDefined(SimplicialModuleMap): isWellDefined_lpSimplicialModuleMap_rp,.

