map(SimplicialModule,SimplicialModule,ZZ) -- make the zero map or identity between simplicial modules
*****************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note map: (Macaulay2Doc)map,
  * Usage: 
        f = map(D, C, 0)
        f = map(C, C, 1)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, 
      * D, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, 
      * 0, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or 1
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degree: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default
        value null, specify the degree of a map of simplicial modules
      * *note DegreeLift: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeLift=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, unused option for maps of simplicial modules
      * *note DegreeMap: map_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegreeMap=>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ...,
        default value null, unused option for maps of simplicial modules
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, the zero
        map from $C$ to $D$ or the identity map from $C$ to $C$

Description
===========

A map of simplicial modules $f : C \rightarrow D$ of degree $d$ is a sequence
of maps $f_i : C_i \rightarrow D_{d+i}$.

We construct the zero map between two simplicial modules.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = simplicialModule(freeResolution coker vars R, Degeneracy => true)   |
|                                                                             |
|      1      4      10      20                                               |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R  <-- ...                                        |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2       3                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : SimplicialModule                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = simplicialModule(freeResolution coker matrix{{a^2, b^2, c^2}},      |
|                                                                             |
|      1      4      10      20                                               |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R  <-- ...                                        |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2       3                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : SimplicialModule                                                        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|Degeneracy => true)                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = map(D, C, 0)                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : SimplicialModuleMap                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert isWellDefined f                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert isSimplicialMorphism f                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : g = map(C, C, 0, Degree => 13)                                          |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = 0                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o7 : SimplicialModuleMap                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert isWellDefined g                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(degree g == 13)                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert not isSimplicialMorphism g                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert isCommutative g                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : assert isHomogeneous g                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert(source g == C)                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert(target g == C)                                                  |
