+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Taking the cokernel of the above morphism yields a canonically defined Schur
functor $\mathbb{S}^{(2,1)} (K)$; constructing this complex using the classical
Schur complex definition will yield a complex that does not have finite length
homology (and hence isn't even homotopically equivalent).

