randomSimplicialMap(SimplicialModule,SimplicialModule) -- a random map of simplicial modules
********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note randomSimplicialMap:
    randomSimplicialMap_lpSimplicialModule_cmSimplicialModule_rp,
  * Usage: 
        f = randomSimplicialMap(C,D)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, 
      * D, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Boundary => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, whether the constructed f is a simplicial null homotopy
      * Cycle => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, whether the constructed f commutes with the face/degeneracy maps
      * Degree => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, the
        degree of the constructed map of simplicial modules
      * InternalDegree => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value
        null, or an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, 

Description
===========

A random simplicial module map $f : C \to D$ is obtained from choosing a random
map of the underlying normalizations, which uses the *note randomComplexMap:
(Complexes)randomComplexMap_lpComplex_cmComplex_rp, command.

