RingMap ** SimplicialModuleMap -- tensor a map of simplicial modules along a ring map
*************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note **: (Macaulay2Doc)_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        phi ** f
        tensor(phi, f)
        S ** f
        f ** S
  * Inputs:
      * phi, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, whose source is a ring
        $R$, and whose target is a ring $S$
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, over the
        ring $R$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, over the ring
        $S$

Description
===========

These methods implement the base change of rings.  As input, one can either
give a ring map $\phi$, or the ring $S$ (when there is a canonical map from $R$
to $S$).

We illustrate the tensor product of a map of simplicial modules along a ring
map.

