SimplicialModuleMap ++ SimplicialModuleMap -- direct sum of simplicial module maps
**********************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ++: (Macaulay2Doc)++,
  * Usage: 
        h = f ++ g
        h = directSum(f,g,...)
        h = directSum(name1 => f, name2 => g, ...)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, 
      * g, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, that is the
        direct sum of the input simplicial module maps

Description
===========

The direct sum of two simplicial module maps is a simplicial module map from
the direct sum of the sources to the direct sum of the targets.

First, we define some non-trivial maps of simplicial modules.

