SimplicialModuleMap == SimplicialModuleMap -- whether two simplicial module maps are equal
******************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        f == g
        f == 0
        f == 1
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, or 0, or 1.
      * g, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, or 0, or 1.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when f and
        g are equal

Description
===========

Two simplicial module maps are equal if they have the same source, the same
target, and $f_i = g_i$ for all $i$.

