SimplicialModuleMap ^ ZZ -- the n-fold composition
**************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        f^n
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, whose
        source and target are the same simplicial module
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, the
        composition of $f$ with itself $n$ times.

Description
===========

A simplicial module map $f : C \to C$ can be composed with itself. This method
produces these new maps of simplicial modules.

The face/degeneracy map always composes with itself to give the zero map.

