simplicialTensor -- compute the simplicial tensor product and cache direct sum indices for easy access
******************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        simplicialTensor(T, Options => {Degeneracy => false, TopDegree => null})
  * Inputs:
      * T, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of simplicial modules or
        complexes to compute the tensor product.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Degeneracy: simplicialTensor_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmDegeneracy=>_pd_pd_pd_
        rp, => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, Default value is false. Indicates whether to include degeneracy
        maps in the construction.
      * *note TopDegree: simplicialTensor_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTopDegree=>_pd_pd_pd_rp
        , => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, Default
        is null. If provided, specifies the top degree for the construction of
        the simplicial module.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, The simplicial tensor
        product of the components in T, with cached direct sum indices.

Description
===========

This function computes the simplicial tensor product of a list T, which can
consist of simplicial modules or complexes. It caches direct sum indices using
*note tensorwithComponents: tensorwithComponents, so that the user can easily
access components of the resulting face/degeneracy maps on particular direct
summands of the tensor product.

The simplicial tensor product of complexes is built as the Dold-Kan extension
of the tensor product functor on the category of R-modules. In general, this
complex looks quite different from the standard tensor product of complexes. In
fact, the simplicial tensor product is always homotopy equivalent to the
classically defined tensor product.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Q = ZZ/101[x_1,x_2];                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : K1 = complex {matrix{{x_1}}};        |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : K2 = complex {matrix{{x_2}}};        |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : T1 = K1**K2                          |
|                                          |
|      1      2      1                     |
|o4 = Q  <-- Q  <-- Q                      |
|                                          |
|     0      1      2                      |
|                                          |
|o4 : Complex                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : T1.dd                                |
|                                          |
|          1                   2           |
|o5 = 0 : Q  <--------------- Q  : 1       |
|               | x_2 x_1 |                |
|                                          |
|          2                    1          |
|     1 : Q  <---------------- Q  : 2      |
|               {1} | x_1  |               |
|               {1} | -x_2 |               |
|                                          |
|o5 : ComplexMap                           |
+------------------------------------------+
|i6 : T2 = prune simplicialTensor({K1,K2}) |
|                                          |
|      1      3      2                     |
|o6 = Q  <-- Q  <-- Q                      |
|                                          |
|     0      1      2                      |
|                                          |
|o6 : Complex                              |
+------------------------------------------+
|i7 : T2.dd                                |
|                                          |
|          1                          3    |
|o7 = 0 : Q  <---------------------- Q  : 1|
|               | x_2 x_1 x_1x_2 |         |
|                                          |
|          3                         2     |
|     1 : Q  <--------------------- Q  : 2 |
