symmetricQuotient -- computes the image of the surjection from the simplicial tensor product onto the second symmetric power of a simplicial module
***************************************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        symmetricQuotient(S)
  * Inputs:
      * S, a *note Simplicial Module: SimplicialModule,, or *note Complex:
        (Complexes)Complex, or *note Module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, optional
        integer argument specifies top degree
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Map of Simplicial Modules: SimplicialModuleMap,, The induced
        map representing the image of the surjection from the simplicial tensor
        product onto the second symmetric power of S.

Description
===========

This function computes the induced map on the cokernel of the map constructed
by the *note exteriorInclusion: exteriorInclusion, method, which is explicitly
giving the map $$S \otimes S \to \operatorname{Sym}^2 (S).$$ Let us see some
examples:

