tensorwithComponents -- compute the tensor product of direct summands, caching the components for easy access
*************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        tensorwithComponents(M, N)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * N, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, Two modules whose tensor
        product of direct summands is to be computed.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, The tensor product of M and N,
        with cached components for easier access

Description
===========

This function computes the tensor product of two modules M and N, but
additionally caches the components based on the component indices of the
original modules. This caching is particularly useful for easily accessing
induced maps on components of tensor products of direct sums.

If M and N have cached index components, then this function will use those
indices. This function is mostly used for extracting components of the
simplicial tensor product, since the full face/degeneracy maps are typically
much too large to be displayed on their own.

